# Google Calendar OAuth Configuration

# To enable Google Calendar integration, you need to create OAuth 2.0 credentials:

## Setup Instructions

1. Go to Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/
2. Create a new project or select an existing one
3. Enable the Google Calendar API:
   - Go to "APIs & Services" > "Library"
   - Search for "Google Calendar API"
   - Click "Enable"

4. Configure OAuth Consent Screen:
   - Go to "APIs & Services" > "OAuth consent screen"
   - Select "External" user type (or "Internal" if using Google Workspace)
   - Fill in required app information
   - Add scope: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
   - Add test users if using External

5. Create OAuth 2.0 Credentials:
   - Go to "APIs & Services" > "Credentials"
   - Click "Create Credentials" > "OAuth client ID"
   - Select "Desktop app" as application type
   - Give it a name (e.g., "Task Manager Desktop")
   - Click "Create"
   - Download the JSON file or copy the Client ID and Client Secret

6. Set environment variables:
   - Copy this file to `.env.local`
   - Replace the placeholder values below with your actual credentials

## Environment Variables

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id-here.apps.googleusercontent.com
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here

## Important Notes

- The redirect URI is configured as: http://localhost:8888/oauth/callback
- Make sure to add this exact URL to your OAuth 2.0 Client's "Authorized redirect URIs"
- Keep your Client Secret secure and never commit it to version control
- Add `.env.local` to your `.gitignore` file

## Testing

After configuration:
1. Start the app: `npm run tauri dev`
2. Go to Calendar tab
3. Click "Connect Google Calendar"
4. Browser will open for authorization
5. After granting access, you'll be redirected back to the app
6. Your calendars and events will sync automatically
